{
  "$description": "Lost in Preparation v2 tokens. Two themes share one set of semantic names: LIGHT = 'Herbarium' (warm paper, aubergine ink, botanical green, saffron) and DARK = 'Nocturne' (night ink, bone, saffron, lilac, verdigris). Each theme also carries its own type system. tokens.css mirrors these values; tailwind.config.ts maps utilities onto the CSS variables. Contrast ratios (WCAG 2.x) are recorded as measured; re-run the check after any change.",
  "$version": "2.0.0",
  "meaning": {
    "brand": "Botanical identity and wayfinding (links, primary actions, focus). NEVER means 'safe' or 'good'.",
    "hist": "The HISTORICAL preparation. Saffron. Filled bands.",
    "mod": "The MODERN lab method. Aubergine (light) / lilac (dark). Drawn as an OUTLINE band or underline, so it separates from saffron by fill style and lightness, not hue alone.",
    "tox": "Toxicity only. Crimson (light) / rose (dark).",
    "unk": "Unknown: neutral grey with a hatch. Never zero, never blank.",
    "prov": "Provisional evidence (AI reference, not human-checked): neutral, dashed border, half-filled glyph. Deliberately NOT the modern-lab hue."
  },
